.TH DISK-FULL-DOCTOR 1 "2026-11-01" "disk-full-doctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
disk-full-doctor \- read-only report of why a disk looks full when df and du disagree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B disk-full-doctor
.RB "[ " --json " ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
disk-full-doctor prints one read-only report for "No space left on device"
when df and du disagree.
The report is sorted by bytes.
It checks deleted_open (deleted-but-open files via /proc/<pid>/fd),
inodes (inode use per mount),
docker_logs (Docker json-file container logs and a missing max-size),
journald (size of /var/log/journal and /run/log/journal, and SystemMaxUse
when journald.conf is readable),
buildkit (Docker BuildKit cache and an external buildkitd cache),
and df_du_gap (per mount, statvfs used bytes next to a du-style sum,
and the gap).
Each finding reports bytes or inodes, one line of evidence, and a short hint.
The tool never deletes, writes, or changes anything, and it never touches
the Docker socket or CLI, lsof, or journalctl.
Without permission to read a path, a check reports NeedsRoot with a
plain-text hint.
The report ends with a summary line naming every check that needs root
to see more.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Print the report as JSON.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print help.
.TP
.BR -V ", " --version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing actionable was found.
No finding has status Warn, NeedsRoot, or Error.
.TP
.B 1
A check reported Warn, NeedsRoot, or Error.
The program also exits 1 when it rejects a path before printing the report.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was rejected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Text report:
.PP
.B disk-full-doctor
.PP
JSON report:
.PP
.B disk-full-doctor --json
.PP
Help and version:
.PP
.B disk-full-doctor --help
.PP
.B disk-full-doctor --version
